      "mergeID": "642d924ebd996c8822da9959",
      "mergedPostDetails": "The portal mode types are named as \"Drop\", and \"Manual\".\n\nThis seems to be confusing, since most players use the term \"drop a portal\" in English.\n\nUnderstandably, 'dropping' usually refers to releasing something in front of you. Since VRChat users are used to the luxury of pointing-and-clicking to 'drop a portal', it might be better to re-name the modes to \"Point\", and \"Instant\".\n\nInstant, meaning that the portal drops instantly in front of the user. Point, meaning that the user must point before dropping the portal.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1292] Suggestion to re-name the 'portal mode' types.",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "642cdbf4246669901d957bfd",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I agree that the current names are pretty unclear, though I'm not convinced the suggested names are an improvement.\n\nThe names \"Drop\" and \"Place\" could be another potential alternative; with \"Drop\" indicating a portal that's just 'dropped' in front of you without exact care for where it lands, and \"Place\" indicating a portal that you 'place' in a specific spot.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
